abstract: >-
  Anti-DDI v3 is an evidence-state framework and benchmark resource for drug
  non-interaction research. The full release contains 797 audited pair records,
  of which 538 T1/T2 records constitute the default evidence-supported Anti-DDI
  benchmark. v3 explicitly separates supported Anti-DDI states from limited
  candidates, unresolved records, structural controls, and positive-concern
  exclusions. It also publishes the frozen Paper 5 development/confirmatory split
  and eight post-confirmatory human clinical-pharmacology anchors. The resource is
  for research and benchmarking and is not a prescribing safety list. It preserves
  the complete v2 audit and provenance trail, including disclosure of the retracted
  predecessor used solely as an audit object.
